\tag{fdip}
\title{Coordinate symmetries of momentum blocks}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{On a periodic grid, shifting a Fourier mode by one site multiplies it
by a scalar. Each coordinate direction has its own multiplier. Reversing
a direction can change its multiplier, and exchanging two directions
can move a field between the momentum blocks of \ref{fdip-000S}.
Which blocks can be reached from one another? Which coordinate symmetries
still act within a single block?}

\transclude{fdip-0162}
\transclude{fdip-016A}
